## Where to look next

### Instructions the runs were served

Each run was served the blueprint as it was at one commit. In a clone of your blueprint repo, `git show <commit>:<path>` prints a file as that run saw it. Routines are in `routines/<name>.md`, skills in `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and rules in `rules/<name>.mdc`; a run's own file lists the skills and rules it loaded.

- `b4c5d6e` (factory acme, 2 runs)
  - `git -C <your blueprint clone> show b4c5d6e:routines/autofix.md`
  - `git -C <your blueprint clone> show b4c5d6e:routines/pr-review.md`

- `ee8f142` (factory acme, 3 runs)
  - `git -C <your blueprint clone> show ee8f142:routines/pr-review.md`

If your blueprint lives in a subfolder of its repo, put that folder in front of the path.

### Pull requests

The review comments on these are often the best sign of what went wrong.

