## Fields you can't fully trust

Agents write the intents, summaries, statuses, friction notes, links and session pointers, on a best-effort basis, so they can be missing, wrong or vague. A run that says `succeeded` may not have. Fabrica writes the times, the blueprint commits, the factory and the loads, so those are reliable, and so are its own refusals.
